{"type":"message","id":"abf16802","parentId":"49471c72","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:54:06.762Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now note: I used `fs` in readJson and writeFile but fs is not defined! I forgot to require fs after moving things. I'll need to require fs as well. Since we're using CommonJS require, I can do `const fs = require('fs');` inside loadExternalModules or at top of main. I'll add it inside loadExternalModules or just require it early because it's built-in and safe. I'll add at the top after the createRequire: also require('fs'). But earlier I had it at top but then moved? Let's just require it early as it's built-in and doesn't need installation. I'll modify the import section to include fs.\n\nBut careful: the script is an ES module because of package.json type. However, we are using createRequire which returns a CommonJS require function that can load built-in modules and CommonJS packages. That should work. So I'll do:\n\nimport { createRequire } from 'module';\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst { spawnSync } = require('child_process');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nBut note: path and child_process are built-ins, but in ESM they can be imported via `import` from 'node:path' etc. However, using require with createRequire should work.\n\nLet's update the top:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I need to include `fs` in the requires. I'll update the top imports:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_292ec21931e0423aae6345f6","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social\\analyze-and-generate.js","old_string":"// Immediately output debug info to stderr (won't interfere with base64 markers)\nconsole.error(`[DEBUG] Script started at ${new Date().toISOString()}`);\n\n// Use createRequire to support CommonJS requires in an ES module context\nimport { createRequire } from 'module';\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n\n// Built-in modules we can require early\nconst { spawnSync } = require('child_process');\nconst path = require('path');","new_string":"// Immediately output debug info to stderr (won't interfere with base64 markers)\nconsole.error(`[DEBUG] Script started at ${new Date().toISOString()}`);\n\n// Use createRequire to support CommonJS requires in an ES module context\nimport { createRequire } from 'module';\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n\n// Built-in modules\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst { spawnSync } = require('child_process');\nconst path = require('path');"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":65027,"output":888,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":65915,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419238660}}
