{"type":"message","id":"53591482","parentId":"4720d0e9","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:54:25.763Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now also, in the loadExternalModules function we need to set the workerSrc. That we had earlier. I already did that: pdfjsLib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = require('pdfjs-dist/legacy/build/pdf.worker.js'); That's fine.\n\nBut note: after loadExternalModules, we should also set the workerSrc. That is done.\n\nNow we need to handle the fact that we used `fs` in readJson and writeFile, which are defined before loadExternalModules, but that's fine because fs is already required at top.\n\nAlso, the function findFile uses fs, that's fine.\n\nOne more: In the script we have `let createCanvas = null; let pdfjsLib = null;` They will be assigned in loadExternalModules. Functions like renderFirstPage and analyzeLayout use them, but they are only called after main invokes loadExternalModules, so they'll be defined.\n\nNow I also need to adjust the require for the slide generator. That will happen inside runSlideGenerator after locateResources. At that point, pdfjsLib and canvas are not needed; only require for the generator. That should work.\n\nNow we must also note that the slide generator itself might be an ES module? If it's .js in a package with \"type\":\"module\", it will be ESM. Our try/catch with require will fail for ESM. But we fallback to spawn. That's fine.\n\nNow run again:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Now run the script with pty again:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_899cc046c4a943cda5b0020a","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"node analyze-and-generate.js","host":"gateway","workdir":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social","pty":true,"background":true,"yieldMs":600000}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":65645,"output":739,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":66384,"cost":{"inpu