{"type":"message","id":"545e4a87","parentId":"1b2f764a","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:54:42.694Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Right, __dirname is also not defined in ES modules. I need to use import.meta.url and convert to a path. In ES modules, to get the directory of the current module, you can use:\n\nconst __filename = import.meta.url.replace('file://', '');\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n\nBut on Windows, need to handle properly. There's also the file URL to path conversion: `new URL(import.meta.url).pathname` and then decode.\n\nSimpler: use `path.dirname(process.argv[1])`? That gives the script path as passed, but may not be absolute. Better: use `import.meta.url` and convert.\n\nI'll define:\n\nconst __filename = new URL(import.meta.url).pathname;\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n\nBut on Windows, pathname will start with '/', e.g., '/D:/workspace/...'. We can strip leading slash and then handle drive letter. Actually new URL('file:///D:/path').pathname gives '/D:/path'. That's fine for path operations? path.dirname('/D:/workspace/...') yields '/D:/workspace/...', which is okay for fs operations because Node accepts posix-style paths on Windows? Usually it normalizes. But better to use `fileURLToPath` from 'url' module.\n\nSo:\n\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'url';\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n\nThat's the proper way.\n\nI'll add that.\n\nAlso need to import 'url'.\n\nLet's update the top.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Need to handle `__dirname` in ES module. I'll use `fileURLToPath`:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3fb09b96cc614c0bbaa039dc","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social\\analyze-and-generate.js","old_string":"// Immediately output debug info to stderr (won't interfere with base64 markers)\nconsole.error(`[DEBUG] Script started at ${new Date().toISOString()}`);\n\n// Use createRequire to support CommonJS requires in an ES module context\nimport { createRequire } from 'module';\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n\n// Built-in modules\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst { spawnSync } = require('child_process');\nconst path = require('path');","new_string":"// Immediately output debug info to stderr (won't interfere with base64 markers)\nconsole.error(`[DEBUG] Script started at ${new Date().toISOString()}`);\n\n// Use createRequire to support CommonJS requires in an ES module context\nimport { createRequire } from 'module';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'url';\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n\n// Built-in modules\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst { spawnSync } = require('child_process');\nconst path = require('path');\n\n// Derive __dirname from import.meta.url (ES module compatibility)\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":66522,"output":1054,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":67576,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419272227}}
