e are only allowed to use host=gateway, not host=host or host=node. But the gateway doesn't have write access to the workspace? Wait, the gateway is part of OpenClaw and likely runs on the same machine as the agent, so it should have same filesystem access. But maybe the gateway runs as a service under a different user with limited permissions.\n\nLet's check the openclaw gateway status. Maybe I can use the gateway to run commands, but I need to ensure the workdir is something like the user's temp. But the slide generator needs to read the example slides and write the PDF. If we set outputPdfPath to a location the gateway can write to, and then we capture the PDF via base64 stdout, we don't need the agent to read that file. That's okay. But the slide generator itself must be able to read the example slides JSON (which is in the workspace) and write the PDF to a path we provide. If the gateway can't read the workspace, it will fail to find the example slides. But we can locate those using findFile, which uses fs.existsSync. If the gateway can't access the workspace, those will return false, and we'll throw \"Could not find example-openclaw-slides.json\". That's plausible.\n\nEarlier, in the output we got past the dependency check? We didn't even get to that because npm install failed. But we saw \"Checking dependencies...\" and then \"npm install failed\". That happened before trying to locate resources.\n\nSo we have two problems:\n1. The gateway cannot install canvas (maybe due to missing build tools OR cannot write to workspace for node_modules creation)\n2. Even if we had canvas, the gateway may not be able to read the workspace for the slide generator.\n\nGiven the severity, maybe the intended execution environment is not the gateway but the node itself, and the policy error indicates we need to configure something to allow exec to node. Perhaps the user (main agent) expects that I, as subagent, will run on the node where the workspace is accessible. The policy message: \"exec host not allowed (requested node; configure tools.exec.host=gateway to allow).\" This is telling me that I tried to use node, which is disallowed, and I should use gateway instead. But gateway is having issues. Maybe I need to configure something to allow node? That would be a configuration change that I'm not supposed to do. The instruction says \"Run quietly, no questions.\" So I shouldn't be asking for config changes. So perhaps the intended host is actually \"gateway\" and the gateway does have access to the workspace, but my earlier attempts to write files failed because the gateway's view of the filesystem is different? The error \"ENOENT\" when reading files suggests the files aren't there, but maybe they are under a different path.\n\nMaybe the gateway's filesystem is the same as the agent's, but my workdir parameter might be wrong. The gateway might resolve the path differently: e.g., D:\\... might not be the correct path because the gateway uses Linux-style paths? But it's Windows, so D:\\ should be fine.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the gateway's CWD is something else and the relative paths are off, but I used absolute paths for CONFIG.themeCssPath and outputPdfPath. Those are absolute. So that should be fine.\n\nBut when I tried to read npm-install.log, it was not found. That suggests the script didn't successfully write it, maybe because the script error occurred before that point? Actually, the log file is written in ensureDependencies if npm runs. Since npm didn't run (or the spawn didn't complete), the file might not be created. However, even if npm ran, we might not have written the log because we only write it after capturing stdout/stderr. If the spawn failed before producing output, the file might be empty or not created. But we also had a writeFile for the CSS later, but that didn't happen.\n\nSo the root issue is that the npm install command failed. Why? It might be due to network issues, or because the gateway's npm is not configured. But the error says exit code null, which is weird. Possibly the spawnSync could not find the npm executable? That would cause an ENOENT error, which might set status to null. Let's test: if we try to spawn a non-existent command, spawnSync returns { pid:..., status: null, signal: null, stdout: '', stderr: '' }? Actually, on Windows, if the command is not found, it returns status 1? Not sure.\n\nMaybe the gateway doesn't have npm in PATH. We could try to use absolute path to npm, like `C:\\Program Files\\nodejs\\npm.cmd`. But not sure.\n\nGiven the complexity, maybe we should avoid using npm install altogether by using prebuilt dependencies? But they are not present.\n\nAnother angle: The task said: \"Install Node.js dependencies: npm install pdfjs-dist canvas (canvas may require build tools; if it fails, we'll use a simpler approach).\" So they anticipate that canvas may fail, and then we'll use a simpler approach. What is the simpler approach? Possibly using a different method to analyze colors and layout without rendering to a canvas. Perhaps we can use pdfjs-dist's text layer and vector data to infer colors and fonts without rasterization? That's still heavy but maybe possible: pdfjs-dist provides the text content with font info and also the fill color for each text item? I think text items have a `fill` property (like fill color) if you set `includeMarkedContent`? Not sure. Actually, pdfjs-dist's textContent.items may include `fill` (like rgb) if you call `page.getTextContent({ includeMarkedContent: true })`? I'm not sure. There's also `page.getAnnotations` etc.\n\nBut dominant colors: we could sample colors from the PDF's internal images (if any) or from the fill colors of text and graphics. That's more complex than pixel sampling.\n\nAlternatively, maybe \"simpler approach\" means we skip the PDF analysis entirely and manual create a theme? But that violates the task.\n\nWait, the task says: \"Write a script that reads the sample PDF at ..., renders the first page to an image using pdfjs-dist, and analyzes dominant colors, approximate font sizes, and layout.\" That's explicit. So we must render to an image. So canvas is required. So we must get canvas working.\n\nMaybe the failure is because the gateway's npm is broken or node version mismatch. Could try to install canvas with a specific version that supports Node 24. Let's check: canvas versions: canvas@2.11.2 is the latest as of 2024; it supports Node up to 20? Actually, canvas 2.11.2 supports Node 12-20. Node 24 might not be supported yet. So canvas may not have prebuilt binaries for Node 24, and building from source fails because it requires older node-gyp compatibility. That could cause failure.\n\nGiven that Node is v24.12.0 (as per runtime), canvas may not support it. We could try to install an older version of canvas that works with Node 24? Not likely; Node 24 is very new. Maybe we can use a different version of Node? But we're stuck with the runtime's node.\n\nMaybe we can use a pure JS alternative to canvas for rasterizing PDF? There is `pdf2pic` which uses pdfjs-dist and canvas. Not helpful.\n\nWhat about using `sharp`? That's image processing, not rendering PDF.\n\nMaybe we can use a headless Chrome to render PDF to PNG. That would require installing puppeteer, which is heavy and also needs a browser. Not simpler.\n\nGiven the time, maybe I should try to install canvas with the `--force` flag or with a specific version that has prebuilt binaries for Node 24? Could be that canvas 3.0 (alpha) supports newer Node. But I'm not sure.\n\nLet's check the error from npm. Since the log file didn't get written, maybe the spawn didn't produce any output because the process didn't even start due to missing npm. On Windows, npm is a .cmd file. spawnSync with 'npm' should work if npm is in PATH. But maybe PATH in the gateway environment is different. Could be that node is available but npm is not in PATH. Node usually installs npm in the same directory (nodejs). So npm should be available as a sibling.\n\nWe could try using `npm.cmd` explicitly or give absolute path. We can detect node's location via `process.execPath` and derive npm path. For example, `path.join(path.dirname(process.execPath), 'npm.cmd')`.\n\nI can modify ensureDependencies to use absolute path to npm:\n\n```javascript\nconst npmPath = process.platform === 'win32' ? path.join(path.dirname(process.execPath), 'npm.cmd') : 'npm';\n```\n\nThat ensures we call the npm that ships with Node.\n\nLet's try that.\n\nAlso, we can try to install with `--verbose` to get more logs.\n\nBut the bigger issue: even if npm installs, canvas might still fail to build. However, we'll see in the logs.\n\nGiven the constraints, I'll proceed to adjust ensureDependencies to use absolute npm path and capture output properly, and also maybe set environment variable to skip optional dependencies? Actually canvas has required dependencies.\n\nWe also need to ensure that the gateway has permission to write to the workspace. It seems likely it does not, because the log file wasn't created. The spawnSync with stdio: 'pipe' captured stdout/stderr, but we then wrote to a file using fs.writeFileSync. That write would have failed if no permission. But we didn't catch that error because we only wrote if result.stdout existed. But if result.stdout is empty because npm didn't start, we wouldn't write the file. But also, if stdout is empty but stderr had something, we would try to write to file. That file write could fail due to permission, but we didn't catch it. We should wrap file writes in try/catch and maybe fall back to console.\n\nBut maybe the gateway can write to the workspace? The earlier test with echo created a file? That also didn't appear. So maybe the gateway cannot write to the workspace. That is a critical problem because the script needs to write the theme CSS and the slide generator needs to write the PDF. However, we don't rely on the agent reading those files; we capture them via base64. But the slide generator still writes the PDF to a file that we then read. That read is within the same gateway environment, so if the gateway can write to its own filesystem, that's fine; the path we give for outputPdfPath is within the workspace. If the gateway cannot write to that path, the slide generator will fail to write the PDF. So we need the gateway to have write access to the workspace.\n\nMaybe the gateway's filesystem is not the same as the agent's, but the workspace is mounted read-only? Or the gateway runs as a service with a different user that lacks write permission to D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social.\n\nI could change the output paths to a temporary directory like the system's temp folder, which should be writable. The slide generator would then write the PDF there, and we can read it and output base64. That might work. Similarly for the theme CSS: we can write it to temp, but the slide generator needs to read that CSS file. So the CSS file must be accessible to the slide generator as well. So we can write both to a temp directory. The script and the slide generator both run in the same environment, so they can access the temp dir.\n\nGreat! That's the solution: Use a temporary directory for intermediate files (theme.css, output.pdf). That avoids permission issues with the workspace. Then we capture the base64 output and the agent writes them to the workspace.\n\nSo I'll modify CONFIG:\n- themeCssPath: path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'openclaw-theme.css')\n- outputPdfPath: path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'openclaw-demo.pdf')\n\nBut we also need the findFile to locate the slide generator and example slides. Those are in the workspace, which may be readable? It might still be readable even if not writable. Typically, read access is easier. So that's okay.\n\nLet's incorporate that.\n\nAlso, we should ensure the temp files are cleaned up? Not necessary.\n\nNow, we also need to ensure that the npm install itself can write to node_modules in the workspace? That still needs write access. But maybe we can also install dependencies into a temporary location? Not ideal; we can do a user install or a custom prefix. But the script requires pdfjs-dist and canvas modules. They need to be in node_modules relative to the script or globally. We could try to install them to a temp directory and set NODE_PATH. That's more complicated.\n\nMaybe we can avoid installing canvas and pdfjs-dist by using the ones already installed globally? But likely not.\n\nAlternatively, we could use a different approach: Since we're on the gateway, maybe the dependencies are already installed? Let's check: The earlier attempt to require('canvas') failed because node_modules not found. That indicates no local node_modules. We could try to install globally with `npm install -g`, but might not have permission.\n\nPerhaps the simplest is to attempt to install to the workspace even if it's read-only, it'll fail. But we could install to a temp directory and then set NODE_PATH accordingly.\n\nLet's modify ensureDependencies to install into a local folder within the temp directory? But we can do:\n\nconst nodeModulesPath = path.join(WORKSPACE_ROOT, 'node_modules'); // we can change to temp.\n\nIf we can't write to workspace, we can set a custom install location using npm's prefix. But that gets messy.\n\nMaybe the gateway actually can write to the workspace; we haven't proven it can't. The echo test didn't produce a file, but maybe because the command's output redirection wasn't captured correctly? Let's re-evaluate: In the echo test, we ran `echo \"sandbox test\" > sandbox_test.txt` with host=\"gateway\" and pty=true. The script then polled and we saw no file. But maybe the file was written to a different location because the working directory of the command was not the workspace, despite workdir param? The workdir param should set the working directory for the command. If we set workdir to workspace, the echo should write there. We did set workdir to the workspace in that test. Did we? Let's check the earlier command: \n\n`exec(command=\"echo \\\"sandbox test\\\" > sandbox_test.txt\", host=\"gateway\", workdir=\"D:\\\\workspace\\\\appDev\\\\openclaw\\\\workspace-social\", pty=True, background=True, yieldMs=2000)`\n\nYes. The file should be there. But read returned ENOENT. That suggests the gateway process's filesystem does not have that file. Could be that the redirection using `>` is a shell feature and the command was run without a shell? When we use pty, the command might be executed via a shell? On Windows, `echo` is a built-in of cmd.exe, so to use redirection we need to run `cmd /c \"echo ... > file\"`. The direct echo command might be interpreted as a program and not use shell redirection. Actually, `echo` is a shell built-in, not an executable. So if we run `echo` directly, the system might try to find an executable named echo.exe, which doesn't exist. But in PowerShell, `echo` is an alias for Write-Output, and redirection `>` works in PowerShell. In our pty test, we saw that the shell used was PowerShell. So `echo \"Hello from gateway\"` worked and output was captured. And redirection `> file` should also work in PowerShell. So that should have created the file. But it didn't. Maybe the PowerShell execution policy or the current user's context redirects to a virtual store? Unclear.\n\nGiven the time, it's safer to assume we can write to a temporary directory that is guaranteed to be writable. The tmpdir is usually accessible.\n\nThus, I'll modify the script to use temp dir for the theme and PDF files. That might avoid permission issues.\n\nLet's update the script accordingly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I suspect the gateway may not have write access to the workspace. I'll change the script to use the system temp directory for intermediate files. Also, I'll capture npm output properly and use absolute path to npm. I'll also add a fallback to use prebuilt canvas if possible. Let's rewrite more robustly:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c6220bd39ac743ae9fde7c7b","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"/**\n * analyze-and-generate.js\n *\n * Analyzes a sample PDF to extract style characteristics (colors, fonts, layout).\n * Generates a Marp CSS theme and uses the openclaw slide generator to create a demo deck.\n * Outputs theme CSS and PDF as base64 via stdout for capture.\n */\n\n// Debug\nconsole.error(`[DEBUG] Script started at ${new Date().toISOString()}`);\n\nimport { createRequire } from 'module';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'url';\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst { spawnSync } = require('child_process');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst os = require('os');\n\n// Derive __dirname\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n\n// Use temp directory for files to avoid permission issues\nconst TEMP_DIR = os.tmpdir();\n\nconst CONFIG = {\n  pdfPath: 'C:\\\\Users\\\\mangs\\\\Desktop\\\\Content Marketing\\\\automated_content\\\\sample_slide\\\\1771414106196.pdf',\n  themeCssPath: path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'openclaw-theme.css'),\n  outputPdfPath: path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'openclaw-demo.pdf'),\n  slideGeneratorSearchNames: ['openclaw-slide-generator.js', 'slide-generator.js', 'generate-slides.js'],\n  exampleSlidesSearchNames: ['example-openclaw-slides.json', 'sample-slides.json', 'slides.json'],\n  // Also search in workspace for resources; we can still use workspace for reading resources\n  workspaceRoot: path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..'), // up to openclaw root\n  slideWidth: 1000,\n  slideHeight: 1200,\n  colorSampleStep: 10,\n  dominantColorCount: 5\n};\n\n// Utility: read JSON\nfunction readJson(filePath) {\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8'));\n  } catch (e) {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\n// Utility: write file\nfunction writeFile(filePath, content) {\n  fs.writeFileSync(filePath, 'utf8', content);\n  console.log(`Wrote file: ${filePath}`);\n}\n\n// Ensure dependencies\nfunction ensureDependencies() {\n  console.log('Checking dependencies...');\n  // We'll try to require canvas; if fails, install to TEMP_DIR node_modules\n  try {\n    require('canvas');\n    console.log('canvas already available.');\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log('canvas not found. Installing dependencies to temp dir...');\n    const installDir = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'openclaw_node_modules');\n    // Ensure the directory exists\n    if (!fs.existsSync(installDir)) fs.mkdirSync(installDir, { recursive: true });\n\n    // Determine npm path\n    const nodeBin = path.dirname(process.execPath);\n    const npmExe = process.platform === 'win32' ? path.join(nodeBin, 'npm.cmd') : 'npm';\n    // Use npm install with prefix to install into installDir\n    const args = ['install', '--prefix', installDir, 'pdfjs-dist', 'canvas'];\n    const result = spawnSync(npmExe, args, { stdio: 'pipe', encoding: 'utf-8' });\n    // Log output to a file for debugging\n    const logPath = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'npm-install.log');\n    if (result.stdout) fs.writeFileSync(logPath, result.stdout);\n    if (result.stderr) fs.appendFileSync(logPath, result.stderr);\n    if (result.status !== 0) {\n      throw new Error(`npm install failed with code ${result.status}. See ${logPath}`);\n    }\n    // Add installDir/node_modules to NODE_PATH so subsequent requires can find them\n    process.env.NODE_PATH = path.join(installDir, 'node_modules');\n    // Also require('module').Module._initPaths()? Might not be needed if NODE_PATH set before requiring.\n    console.log('Dependencies installed to', installDir);\n  }\n}\n\n// Load external modules (after ensureDependencies)\nlet createCanvas = null;\nlet pdfjsLib = null;\nfunction loadExternalModules() {\n  // Now require canvas and pdfjs-dist\n  const canvasModule = require('canvas');\n  createCanvas = canvasModule.createCanvas;\n  pdfjsLib = require('pdfjs-dist/legacy/build/pdf.js');\n  pdfjsLib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = require('pdfjs-dist/legacy/build/pdf.worker.js');\n  console.log('External modules loaded.');\n}\n\n// Check PDF exists\nfunction checkPdfExists() {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(CONFIG.pdfPath)) {\n    throw new Error(`Sample PDF not found at: ${CONFIG.pdfPath}`);\n  }\n  console.log(`PDF found: ${CONFIG.pdfPath}`);\n}\n\n// Render first page\nasync function renderFirstPage() {\n  console.log('Loading PDF...');\n  const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument(CONFIG.pdfPath);\n  const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\n  console.log(`PDF loaded: ${pdf.numPages} pages.`);\n  const page = await pdf.getPage(1);\n  const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1.0 });\n  const canvas = createCanvas(viewport.width, viewport.height);\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n  await page.render({ canvasContext: ctx, viewport }).promise;\n  console.log('First page rendered to canvas.');\n  const imageData = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  return { data: imageData.data, width: canvas.width, height: canvas.height };\n}\n\n// Analyze colors\nfunction analyzeColors(imageData) {\n  const { data, width, height } = imageData;\n  const colorMap = new Map();\n  console.log('Sampling colors...');\n  for (let y = 0; y < height; y += CONFIG.colorSampleStep) {\n    for (let x = 0; x < width; x += CONFIG.colorSampleStep) {\n      const i = (y * width + x) * 4;\n      const r = data[i], g = data[i+1], b = data[i+2], a = data[i+3];\n      if (a < 128) continue;\n      const qr = Math.round(r / 16) * 16;\n      const qg = Math.round(g / 16) * 16;\n      const qb = Math.round(b / 16) * 16;\n      const key = `${qr},${qg},${qb}`;\n      colorMap.set(key, (colorMap.get(key) || 0) + 1);\n    }\n  }\n  const sorted = Array.from(colorMap.entries())\n    .sort((a,b) => b[1] - a[1])\n    .slice(0, CONFIG.dominantColorCount * 2);\n  const dominant = sorted.slice(0, CONFIG.dominantColorCount).map(([key]) => {\n    const [r,g,b] = key.split(',').map(Number);\n    return { r, g, b };\n  });\n  console.log(`Found ${dominant.length} dominant colors.`);\n  return dominant;\n}\n\n// Analyze layout\nasync function analyzeLayout() {\n  console.log('Analyzing layout and fonts...');\n  const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument(CONFIG.pdfPath);\n  const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\n  const page = await pdf.getPage(1);\n  const textContent = await page.getTextContent();\n  const items = textContent.items;\n\n  const fontSizes = new Set();\n  const fontNames = new Set();\n  const positions = [];\n\n  items.forEach(item => {\n    if (item.fontSize) fontSizes.add(Math.round(item.fontSize));\n    if (item.fontName) fontNames.add(item.fontName);\n    const x = item.transform ? item.transform[4] : 0;\n    const y = item.transform ? item.transform[5] : 0;\n    positions.push({ x, y, fontSize: item.fontSize || null, fontName: item.fontName || null });\n  });\n\n  let typicalFontSize = 24;\n  const sizesArray = Array.from(fontSizes).filter(s => s > 0);\n  if (sizesArray.length > 0) {\n    sizesArray.sort((a,b) => a-b);\n    typicalFontSize = sizesArray[Math.floor(sizesArray.length/2)];\n  }\n\n  let primaryFontFamily = 'sans-serif';\n  if (fontNames.size > 0) {\n    const rawFont = fontNames.values().next().value;\n    primaryFontFamily = rawFont.split('-')[0].replace(/^[\"']+|[\"']+$/g, '');\n  }\n\n  let margins = null;\n  if (positions.length > 0) {\n    const xs = positions.map(p => p.x);\n    const ys = positions.map(p => p.y);\n    const minX = Math.min(...xs), maxX = Math.max(...xs);\n    const minY = Math.min(...ys), maxY = Math.max(...ys);\n    const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1 });\n    const pageWidth = viewport.width, pageHeight = viewport.height;\n    margins = { left: minX, right: pageWidth - maxX, top: pageHeight - maxY, bottom: minY };\n    console.log(`Margins: left=${margins.left.toFixed(1)}, right=${margins.right.toFixed(1)}, top=${margins.top.toFixed(1)}, bottom=${margins.bottom.toFixed(1)}`);\n  }\n\n  console.log(`Font sizes: ${sizesArray.join(', ')}. Typical: ${typicalFontSize}`);\n  console.log(`Primary font: ${primaryFontFamily}`);\n\n  return { typicalFontSize, primaryFontFamily, margins, textCount: items.length };\n}\n\n// Generate CSS theme\nfunction generateTheme(dominantColors, layoutInfo) {\n  console.log('Generating theme CSS...');\n  const getLuminance = c => 0.299*c.r + 0.587*c.g + 0.114*c.b;\n  const toHex = c => '#' + [c.r, c.g, c.b].map(x => x.toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join('');\n\n  const topColor = dominantColors[0];\n  const secondColor = dominantColors[1];\n  const thirdColor = dominantColors[2];\n  const topLum = getLuminance(topColor);\n\n  let backgroundColor, textColor, accentColor, secondaryColor;\n  if (topLum > 128) {\n    backgroundColor = toHex(topColor);\n    textColor = '#222222';\n    accentColor = secondColor ? toHex(secondColor) : '#0066cc';\n    secondaryColor = thirdColor ? toHex(thirdColor) : '#ff6600';\n  } else {\n    backgroundColor = toHex(topColor);\n    textColor = '#eeeeee';\n    accentColor = secondColor ? toHex(secondColor) : '#4da6ff';\n    secondaryColor = thirdColor ? toHex(thirdColor) : '#ff9933';\n  }\n\n  const baseFontSize = Math.round(layoutInfo.typicalFontSize * 0.7);\n  const headerScale = 1.8;\n  const padH = Math.round(layoutInfo.margins ? layoutInfo.margins.left * 0.5 : 50);\n  const padV = Math.round(layoutInfo.margins ? layoutInfo.margins.right * 0.5 : 50);\n\n  const css = `@theme \"custom-from-pdf\";\nsection {\n  width: ${CONFIG.slideWidth}px;\n  height: ${CONFIG.slideHeight}px;\n  background-color: ${backgroundColor};\n  color: ${textColor};\n  font-family: \"${layoutInfo.primaryFontFamily}\", sans-serif;\n  font-size: ${baseFontSize}px;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  padding: ${padH}px ${padV}px;\n}\nh1, h2, h3 { color: ${accentColor}; font-weight: bold; }\nh1 { font-size: ${Math.round(baseFontSize * headerScale)}px; margin-bottom: 0.5em; }\nh2 { font-size: ${Math.round(baseFontSize * headerScale * 0.85)}px; }\nh3 { font-size: ${Math.round(baseFontSize * headerScale * 0.7)}px; }\na { color: ${accentColor}; }\nmark, blockquote {\n  background-color: ${secondaryColor}33;\n  border-left: 4px solid ${secondaryColor};\n  padding: 0.2em 0.5em;\n}\n`;\n  writeFile(CONFIG.themeCssPath, css);\n  console.log('Theme CSS generated.');\n  return css;\n}\n\n// Find file in workspace (search upward from workspace root)\nfunction findFile(searchNames, startDir = CONFIG.workspaceRoot) {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(startDir)) return null;\n  let dir = startDir;\n  const maxDepth = 5;\n  for (let depth = 0; depth < maxDepth; depth++) {\n    for (const name of searchNames) {\n      const candidate = path.join(dir, name);\n      if (fs.existsSync(candidate)) return candidate;\n    }\n    const parent = path.dirname(dir);\n    if (parent === dir) break;\n    dir = parent;\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\n// Locate resources\nfunction locateResources() {\n  console.log('Locating slide generator and example slides...');\n  const generatorPath = findFile(CONFIG.slideGeneratorSearchNames);\n  const exampleSlidesPath = findFile(CONFIG.exampleSlidesSearchNames);\n  if (!generatorPath) throw new Error('Could not find openclaw-slide-generator.js');\n  if (!exampleSlidesPath) throw new Error('Could not find example-openclaw-slides.json');\n  console.log(`Found generator: ${generatorPath}`);\n  console.log(`Found example slides: ${exampleSlidesPath}`);\n  return { generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath };\n}\n\n// Run slide generator\nfunction runSlideGenerator(generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath, themePath, outputPdfPath) {\n  console.log('Running slide generator...');\n  try {\n    const generator = require(generatorPath);\n    if (typeof generator.generate === 'function') {\n      const slides = readJson(exampleSlidesPath);\n      if (!slides) throw new Error('Failed to parse example slides JSON');\n      generator.generate(slides, themePath, outputPdfPath);\n      console.log('Slide generation via require() succeeded.');\n      return;\n    }\n    throw new Error('Generator does not export generate()');\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log(`Falling back to spawn: node ${generatorPath}`);\n    const args = [generatorPath, '--input', exampleSlidesPath, '--theme', themePath, '--output', outputPdfPath];\n    const result = spawnSync('node', args, { cwd: CONFIG.workspaceRoot, stdio: 'inherit' });\n    if (result.status !== 0) {\n      throw new Error(`Slide generator exited with code ${result.status}`);\n    }\n    console.log('Slide generation via spawn succeeded.');\n  }\n}\n\n// Main\nasync function main() {\n  console.log('=== Starting PDF analysis and slide generation ===');\n  let themeCssContent = null;\n  let pdfContent = null;\n\n  try {\n    ensureDependencies();\n    loadExternalModules();\n    checkPdfExists();\n\n    const imageData = await renderFirstPage();\n    const dominantColors = analyzeColors(imageData);\n    console.log('Dominant colors:', dominantColors.map(c => `rgb(${c.r},${c.g},${c.b})`).join(', '));\n\n    const layoutInfo = await analyzeLayout();\n    console.log('Layout info:', JSON.stringify(layoutInfo, null, 2));\n\n    const css = generateTheme(dominantColors, layoutInfo);\n    themeCssContent = css;\n\n    const { generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath } = locateResources();\n    runSlideGenerator(generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath, CONFIG.themeCssPath, CONFIG.outputPdfPath);\n\n    if (!fs.existsSync(CONFIG.outputPdfPath)) {\n      throw new Error('Slide generator did not produce output PDF');\n    }\n    pdfContent = fs.readFileSync(CONFIG.outputPdfPath);\n    console.log('PDF generated, size:', pdfContent.length, 'bytes');\n\n    // Output base64 for agent capture\n    console.log('\\n===THEME_CSS_BASE64===');\n    console.log(Buffer.from(themeCssContent).toString('base64'));\n    console.log('\\n===PDF_BASE64===');\n    console.log(pdfContent.toString('base64'));\n    console.log('\\n===STATUS===SUCCESS');\n    console.log('Completed successfully.');\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error('\\n===STATUS===ERROR');\n    console.error(err.message);\n    console.error(err.stack);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n\nmain();\n","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social\\analyze-and-generate.js"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":74262,"output":12151,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86413,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419338307}}
{"type":"message","id":"4d7361a7","parentId":"3414e4f5","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:56:22.126Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c6220bd39ac743ae9fde7c7b","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 13670 bytes to D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social\\analyze-and-generate.js"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771419382123}}
{"type":"message","id":"bf519fed","parentId":"4d7361a7","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:56:54.001Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now we're using temp dir for the CSS and PDF, which should be writable. Dependencies are installed to temp as well, with NODE_PATH set. However, requiring modules after setting NODE_PATH might not automatically pick up because the module cache is already initialized. We set NODE_PATH after we already attempted require('canvas') and that failed. In ensureDependencies, we catch the error and then install, set NODE_PATH. After that, we call loadExternalModules which does `require('canvas')`. At that point, the NODE_PATH environment variable is set. Node's module resolution uses process.env.NODE_PATH at startup? Actually, Node reads NODE_PATH at startup and adds those paths to the module search paths. Setting it later might not affect the module search paths. I need to either set NODE_PATH before any require or use `module.Module._initPaths()` after setting. Alternatively, we could directly require with a path: `require(path.join(installDir, 'node_modules', 'canvas'))`. That's simpler: after installation, we can set a variable for the installDir and then require using absolute paths.\n\nI'll modify: after install, we know installDir. We'll store it in a variable accessible to loadExternalModules. Then in loadExternalModules, we'll do:\n\nconst canvasModule = require(path.join(installDir, 'node_modules', 'canvas'));\n\nSimilarly for pdfjs-dist.\n\nLet's incorporate that.\n\nAlso, ensureDependencies returns the installDir or sets a global.\n\nI'll adjust:\n\nlet NODE_INSTALL_DIR = null;\n\nfunction ensureDependencies() {\n  try {\n    require('canvas');\n    console.log('canvas already available.');\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log('canvas not found. Installing dependencies to temp dir...');\n    const installDir = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'openclaw_node_modules');\n    if (!fs.existsSync(installDir)) fs.mkdirSync(installDir, { recursive: true });\n    const nodeBin = path.dirname(process.execPath);\n    const npmExe = process.platform === 'win32' ? path.join(nodeBin, 'npm.cmd') : 'npm';\n    const args = ['install', '--prefix', installDir, 'pdfjs-dist', 'canvas'];\n    const result = spawnSync(npmExe, args, { stdio: 'pipe', encoding: 'utf-8' });\n    const logPath = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'npm-install.log');\n    if (result.stdout) fs.writeFileSync(logPath, result.stdout);\n    if (result.stderr) fs.appendFileSync(logPath, result.stderr);\n    if (result.status !== 0) {\n      throw new Error(`npm install failed with code ${result.status}. See ${logPath}`);\n    }\n    NODE_INSTALL_DIR = installDir;\n    console.log('Dependencies installed to', installDir);\n  }\n}\n\nThen loadExternalModules:\n\nfunction loadExternalModules() {\n  if (NODE_INSTALL_DIR) {\n    // Use absolute requires\n    const canvasPath = path.join(NODE_INSTALL_DIR, 'node_modules', 'canvas');\n    const pdfjsPath = path.join(NODE_INSTALL_DIR, 'node_modules', 'pdfjs-dist', 'legacy', 'build', 'pdf.js');\n    const canvasModule = require(canvasPath);\n    createCanvas = canvasModule.createCanvas;\n    pdfjsLib = require(pdfjsPath);\n  } else {\n    // Use normal require (already available)\n    const canvasModule = require('canvas');\n    createCanvas = canvasModule.createCanvas;\n    pdfjsLib = require('pdfjs-dist/legacy/build/pdf.js');\n  }\n  pdfjsLib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = require('pdfjs-dist/legacy/build/pdf.worker.js');\n  console.log('External modules loaded.');\n}\n\nBut careful: the `require('pdfjs-dist/legacy/build/pdf.worker.js')` should also be resolved from the install dir if we used custom install. The above uses default require, which might still find it from the installDir if we also set NODE_PATH or adjust module paths. I can also require it via absolute path: path.join(NODE_INSTALL_DIR, 'node_modules', 'pdfjs-dist', 'legacy', 'build', 'pdf.worker.js'). But that file might be the worker; we can assign it directly.\n\nBetter: we can set `process.env.NODE_PATH = path.join(NODE_INSTALL_DIR, 'node_modules');` before calling require, and then call `require('module').Module._initPaths();` to refresh the module search paths. That may be simpler.\n\nLet's do that: after setting NODE_INSTALL_DIR, set process.env.NODE_PATH = path.join(NODE_INSTALL_DIR, 'node_modules'); and then call `require('module').Module._initPaths();`. This will cause subsequent require calls to include that path.\n\nBut we have to be careful because require('module') might be cached; but we can do it.\n\nI'll do that in ensureDependencies after install.\n\nSimplify: We'll set NODE_PATH and then call:\n\nconst Module = require('module');\nModule._initPaths();\n\nThis will rebuild the module search paths based on NODE_PATH.\n\nThen loadExternalModules can just require('canvas') etc.\n\nLet's implement that.\n\nAlso, note: In loadExternalModules we also need to require pdfjs-dist/legacy/build/pdf.worker.js. That's fine.\n\nNow update the script accordingly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll refine the dependency installation to install to a temp directory and adjust module resolution:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_69ad482d399b477da2d43c6a","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"/**\n * analyze-and-generate.js\n *\n * Analyzes a sample PDF to extract style characteristics (colors, fonts, layout).\n * Generates a Marp CSS theme and uses the openclaw slide generator to create a demo deck.\n * Outputs theme CSS and PDF as base64 via stdout for capture.\n */\n\n// Debug\nconsole.error(`[DEBUG] Script started at ${new Date().toISOString()}`);\n\nimport { createRequire } from 'module';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'url';\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst { spawnSync } = require('child_process');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst os = require('os');\n\n// Derive __dirname\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n\n// Use temp directory for files to avoid permission issues\nconst TEMP_DIR = os.tmpdir();\n\nlet NODE_INSTALL_DIR = null;\n\nconst CONFIG = {\n  pdfPath: 'C:\\\\Users\\\\mangs\\\\Desktop\\\\Content Marketing\\\\automated_content\\\\sample_slide\\\\1771414106196.pdf',\n  themeCssPath: path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'openclaw-theme.css'),\n  outputPdfPath: path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'openclaw-demo.pdf'),\n  slideGeneratorSearchNames: ['openclaw-slide-generator.js', 'slide-generator.js', 'generate-slides.js'],\n  exampleSlidesSearchNames: ['example-openclaw-slides.json', 'sample-slides.json', 'slides.json'],\n  workspaceRoot: path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..'), // up to openclaw root\n  slideWidth: 1000,\n  slideHeight: 1200,\n  colorSampleStep: 10,\n  dominantColorCount: 5\n};\n\n// Utility: read JSON\nfunction readJson(filePath) {\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8'));\n  } catch (e) {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\n// Utility: write file\nfunction writeFile(filePath, content) {\n  fs.writeFileSync(filePath, 'utf8', content);\n  console.log(`Wrote file: ${filePath}`);\n}\n\n// Ensure dependencies\nfunction ensureDependencies() {\n  console.log('Checking dependencies...');\n  try {\n    require('canvas');\n    console.log('canvas already available.');\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log('canvas not found. Installing dependencies to temp dir...');\n    const installDir = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'openclaw_node_modules');\n    if (!fs.existsSync(installDir)) fs.mkdirSync(installDir, { recursive: true });\n\n    const nodeBin = path.dirname(process.execPath);\n    const npmExe = process.platform === 'win32' ? path.join(nodeBin, 'npm.cmd') : 'npm';\n    const args = ['install', '--prefix', installDir, 'pdfjs-dist', 'canvas'];\n    const result = spawnSync(npmExe, args, { stdio: 'pipe', encoding: 'utf-8' });\n    const logPath = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'npm-install.log');\n    if (result.stdout) fs.writeFileSync(logPath, result.stdout);\n    if (result.stderr) fs.appendFileSync(logPath, result.stderr);\n    if (result.status !== 0) {\n      throw new Error(`npm install failed with code ${result.status}. See ${logPath}`);\n    }\n    NODE_INSTALL_DIR = installDir;\n    // Add to NODE_PATH and re-init module paths\n    process.env.NODE_PATH = path.join(installDir, 'node_modules');\n    const Module = require('module');\n    Module._initPaths();\n    console.log('Dependencies installed and module paths updated.');\n  }\n}\n\n// Load external modules\nlet createCanvas = null;\nlet pdfjsLib = null;\nfunction loadExternalModules() {\n  const canvasModule = require('canvas');\n  createCanvas = canvasModule.createCanvas;\n  pdfjsLib = require('pdfjs-dist/legacy/build/pdf.js');\n  pdfjsLib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = require('pdfjs-dist/legacy/build/pdf.worker.js');\n  console.log('External modules loaded.');\n}\n\n// Check PDF exists\nfunction checkPdfExists() {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(CONFIG.pdfPath)) {\n    throw new Error(`Sample PDF not found at: ${CONFIG.pdfPath}`);\n  }\n  console.log(`PDF found: ${CONFIG.pdfPath}`);\n}\n\n// Render first page\nasync function renderFirstPage() {\n  console.log('Loading PDF...');\n  const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument(CONFIG.pdfPath);\n  const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\n  console.log(`PDF loaded: ${pdf.numPages} pages.`);\n  const page = await pdf.getPage(1);\n  const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1.0 });\n  const canvas = createCanvas(viewport.width, viewport.height);\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n  await page.render({ canvasContext: ctx, viewport }).promise;\n  console.log('First page rendered to canvas.');\n  const imageData = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  return { data: imageData.data, width: canvas.width, height: canvas.height };\n}\n\n// Analyze colors\nfunction analyzeColors(imageData) {\n  const { data, width, height } = imageData;\n  const colorMap = new Map();\n  console.log('Sampling colors...');\n  for (let y = 0; y < height; y += CONFIG.colorSampleStep) {\n    for (let x = 0; x < width; x += CONFIG.colorSampleStep) {\n      const i = (y * width + x) * 4;\n      const r = data[i], g = data[i+1], b = data[i+2], a = data[i+3];\n      if (a < 128) continue;\n      const qr = Math.round(r / 16) * 16;\n      const qg = Math.round(g / 16) * 16;\n      const qb = Math.round(b / 16) * 16;\n      const key = `${qr},${qg},${qb}`;\n      colorMap.set(key, (colorMap.get(key) || 0) + 1);\n    }\n  }\n  const sorted = Array.from(colorMap.entries())\n    .sort((a,b) => b[1] - a[1])\n    .slice(0, CONFIG.dominantColorCount * 2);\n  const dominant = sorted.slice(0, CONFIG.dominantColorCount).map(([key]) => {\n    const [r,g,b] = key.split(',').map(Number);\n    return { r, g, b };\n  });\n  console.log(`Found ${dominant.length} dominant colors.`);\n  return dominant;\n}\n\n// Analyze layout\nasync function analyzeLayout() {\n  console.log('Analyzing layout and fonts...');\n  const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument(CONFIG.pdfPath);\n  const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\n  const page = await pdf.getPage(1);\n  const textContent = await page.getTextContent();\n  const items = textContent.items;\n\n  const fontSizes = new Set();\n  const fontNames = new Set();\n  const positions = [];\n\n  items.forEach(item => {\n    if (item.fontSize) fontSizes.add(Math.round(item.fontSize));\n    if (item.fontName) fontNames.add(item.fontName);\n    const x = item.transform ? item.transform[4] : 0;\n    const y = item.transform ? item.transform[5] : 0;\n    positions.push({ x, y, fontSize: item.fontSize || null, fontName: item.fontName || null });\n  });\n\n  let typicalFontSize = 24;\n  const sizesArray = Array.from(fontSizes).filter(s => s > 0);\n  if (sizesArray.length > 0) {\n    sizesArray.sort((a,b) => a-b);\n    typicalFontSize = sizesArray[Math.floor(sizesArray.length/2)];\n  }\n\n  let primaryFontFamily = 'sans-serif';\n  if (fontNames.size > 0) {\n    const rawFont = fontNames.values().next().value;\n    primaryFontFamily = rawFont.split('-')[0].replace(/^[\"']+|[\"']+$/g, '');\n  }\n\n  let margins = null;\n  if (positions.length > 0) {\n    const xs = positions.map(p => p.x);\n    const ys = positions.map(p => p.y);\n    const minX = Math.min(...xs), maxX = Math.max(...xs);\n    const minY = Math.min(...ys), maxY = Math.max(...ys);\n    const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1 });\n    const pageWidth = viewport.width, pageHeight = viewport.height;\n    margins = { left: minX, right: pageWidth - maxX, top: pageHeight - maxY, bottom: minY };\n    console.log(`Margins: left=${margins.left.toFixed(1)}, right=${margins.right.toFixed(1)}, top=${margins.top.toFixed(1)}, bottom=${margins.bottom.toFixed(1)}`);\n  }\n\n  console.log(`Font sizes: ${sizesArray.join(', ')}. Typical: ${typicalFontSize}`);\n  console.log(`Primary font: ${primaryFontFamily}`);\n\n  return { typicalFontSize, primaryFontFamily, margins, textCount: items.length };\n}\n\n// Generate CSS theme\nfunction generateTheme(dominantColors, layoutInfo) {\n  console.log('Generating theme CSS...');\n  const getLuminance = c => 0.299*c.r + 0.587*c.g + 0.114*c.b;\n  const toHex = c => '#' + [c.r, c.g, c.b].map(x => x.toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join('');\n\n  const topColor = dominantColors[0];\n  const secondColor = dominantColors[1];\n  const thirdColor = dominantColors[2];\n  const topLum = getLuminance(topColor);\n\n  let backgroundColor, textColor, accentColor, secondaryColor;\n  if (topLum > 128) {\n    backgroundColor = toHex(topColor);\n    textColor = '#222222';\n    accentColor = secondColor ? toHex(secondColor) : '#0066cc';\n    secondaryColor = thirdColor ? toHex(thirdColor) : '#ff6600';\n  } else {\n    backgroundColor = toHex(topColor);\n    textColor = '#eeeeee';\n    accentColor = secondColor ? toHex(secondColor) : '#4da6ff';\n    secondaryColor = thirdColor ? toHex(thirdColor) : '#ff9933';\n  }\n\n  const baseFontSize = Math.round(layoutInfo.typicalFontSize * 0.7);\n  const headerScale = 1.8;\n  const padH = Math.round(layoutInfo.margins ? layoutInfo.margins.left * 0.5 : 50);\n  const padV = Math.round(layoutInfo.margins ? layoutInfo.margins.right * 0.5 : 50);\n\n  const css = `@theme \"custom-from-pdf\";\nsection {\n  width: ${CONFIG.slideWidth}px;\n  height: ${CONFIG.slideHeight}px;\n  background-color: ${backgroundColor};\n  color: ${textColor};\n  font-family: \"${layoutInfo.primaryFontFamily}\", sans-serif;\n  font-size: ${baseFontSize}px;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  padding: ${padH}px ${padV}px;\n}\nh1, h2, h3 { color: ${accentColor}; font-weight: bold; }\nh1 { font-size: ${Math.round(baseFontSize * headerScale)}px; margin-bottom: 0.5em; }\nh2 { font-size: ${Math.round(baseFontSize * headerScale * 0.85)}px; }\nh3 { font-size: ${Math.round(baseFontSize * headerScale * 0.7)}px; }\na { color: ${accentColor}; }\nmark, blockquote {\n  background-color: ${secondaryColor}33;\n  border-left: 4px solid ${secondaryColor};\n  padding: 0.2em 0.5em;\n}\n`;\n  writeFile(CONFIG.themeCssPath, css);\n  console.log('Theme CSS generated.');\n  return css;\n}\n\n// Find file in workspace (search upward from workspace root)\nfunction findFile(searchNames, startDir = CONFIG.workspaceRoot) {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(startDir)) return null;\n  let dir = startDir;\n  const maxDepth = 5;\n  for (let depth = 0; depth < maxDepth; depth++) {\n    for (const name of searchNames) {\n      const candidate = path.join(dir, name);\n      if (fs.existsSync(candidate)) return candidate;\n    }\n    const parent = path.dirname(dir);\n    if (parent === dir) break;\n    dir = parent;\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\n// Locate resources\nfunction locateResources() {\n  console.log('Locating slide generator and example slides...');\n  const generatorPath = findFile(CONFIG.slideGeneratorSearchNames);\n  const exampleSlidesPath = findFile(CONFIG.exampleSlidesSearchNames);\n  if (!generatorPath) throw new Error('Could not find openclaw-slide-generator.js');\n  if (!exampleSlidesPath) throw new Error('Could not find example-openclaw-slides.json');\n  console.log(`Found generator: ${generatorPath}`);\n  console.log(`Found example slides: ${exampleSlidesPath}`);\n  return { generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath };\n}\n\n// Run slide generator\nfunction runSlideGenerator(generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath, themePath, outputPdfPath) {\n  console.log('Running slide generator...');\n  try {\n    const generator = require(generatorPath);\n    if (typeof generator.generate === 'function') {\n      const slides = readJson(exampleSlidesPath);\n      if (!slides) throw new Error('Failed to parse example slides JSON');\n      generator.generate(slides, themePath, outputPdfPath);\n      console.log('Slide generation via require() succeeded.');\n      return;\n    }\n    throw new Error('Generator does not export generate()');\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log(`Falling back to spawn: node ${generatorPath}`);\n    // For spawn, ensure the generator can find its modules; it will use its own directory's node_modules?\n    // We set NODE_PATH globally, so it should find dependencies.\n    const args = [generatorPath, '--input', exampleSlidesPath, '--theme', themePath, '--output', outputPdfPath];\n    const result = spawnSync('node', args, { cwd: CONFIG.workspaceRoot, stdio: 'inherit' });\n    if (result.status !== 0) {\n      throw new Error(`Slide generator exited with code ${result.status}`);\n    }\n    console.log('Slide generation via spawn succeeded.');\n  }\n}\n\n// Main\nasync function main() {\n  console.log('=== Starting PDF analysis and slide generation ===');\n  let themeCssContent = null;\n  let pdfContent = null;\n\n  try {\n    ensureDependencies();\n    loadExternalModules();\n    checkPdfExists();\n\n    const imageData = await renderFirstPage();\n    const dominantColors = analyzeColors(imageData);\n    console.log('Dominant colors:', dominantColors.map(c => `rgb(${c.r},${c.g},${c.b})`).join(', '));\n\n    const layoutInfo = await analyzeLayout();\n    console.log('Layout info:', JSON.stringify(layoutInfo, null, 2));\n\n    const css = generateTheme(dominantColors, layoutInfo);\n    themeCssContent = css;\n\n    const { generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath } = locateResources();\n    runSlideGenerator(generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath, CONFIG.themeCssPath, CONFIG.outputPdfPath);\n\n    if (!fs.existsSync(CONFIG.outputPdfPath)) {\n      throw new Error('Slide generator did not produce output PDF');\n    }\n    pdfContent = fs.readFileSync(CONFIG.outputPdfPath);\n    console.log('PDF generated, size:', pdfContent.length, 'bytes');\n\n    // Output base64 for agent capture\n    console.log('\\n===THEME_CSS_BASE64===');\n    console.log(Buffer.from(themeCssContent).toString('base64'));\n    console.log('\\n===PDF_BASE64===');\n    console.log(pdfContent.toString('base64'));\n    console.log('\\n===STATUS===SUCCESS');\n    console.log('Completed successfully.');\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error('\\n===STATUS===ERROR');\n    console.error(err.message);\n    console.error(err.stack);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n\nmain();\n","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social\\analyze-and-generate.js"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":82039,"output":6188,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":88227,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419382127}}
