e for Node 24, it attempts to build and fails. That might be the root cause. But we haven't even seen the attempt because npm didn't spawn.\n\nActually, the failure with code null indicates that the npm command could not be executed. That is separate from build failure. It might be that `npm.cmd` cannot be found because the path contains spaces? We constructed `path.join(nodeBin, 'npm.cmd')`. If nodeBin is \"C:\\Program Files\\nodejs\", then npm.cmd is there. But spawnSync might need to be called with shell = true to run .cmd files? On Windows, to run a .cmd or .bat, you need to specify `cmd.exe /c` or set `shell: true`. However, spawnSync's first argument is the command; if it's an executable (like node.exe), it works directly. For .cmd, you need to run `cmd /c npm.cmd`. So our npmExe should be `cmd` and args `['/c', 'npm.cmd', ...]`. That might be the issue.\n\nI can fix by using `shell: true` option in spawnSync. According to Node.js docs, if you want to run a batch file, you can either explicitly run cmd or set `shell: true`. spawnSync has an option `shell` (boolean or string) to run the command in a shell. I'll set `shell: true`. Then I can pass the command as 'npm' and it will be looked up in the shell. That's simpler.\n\nSo: `spawnSync('npm', args, { cwd: ..., stdio: 'pipe', encoding: 'utf-8', shell: true })`.\n\nThat should handle .cmd.\n\nLet's adjust ensureDependencies to use shell:true.\n\nAlso, we need to capture the output. We'll keep that.\n\nLet's implement that change in the script.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"The npm spawn may need `shell: true` on Windows. I'll update ensureDependencies:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_191391bc00f44e8fbf192a13","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social\\analyze-and-generate.js","old_string":"// Ensure dependencies\nfunction ensureDependencies() {\n  console.log('Checking dependencies...');\n  try {\n    require('canvas');\n    console.log('canvas already available.');\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log('canvas not found. Installing dependencies to temp dir...');\n    const installDir = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'openclaw_node_modules');\n    if (!fs.existsSync(installDir)) fs.mkdirSync(installDir, { recursive: true });\n\n    const nodeBin = path.dirname(process.execPath);\n    const npmExe = process.platform === 'win32' ? path.join(nodeBin, 'npm.cmd') : 'npm';\n    const args = ['install', '--prefix', installDir, 'pdfjs-dist', 'canvas'];\n    const result = spawnSync(npmExe, args, { stdio: 'pipe', encoding: 'utf-8' });\n    const logPath = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'npm-install.log');\n    if (result.stdout) fs.writeFileSync(logPath, result.stdout);\n    if (result.stderr) fs.appendFileSync(logPath, result.stderr);\n    if (result.status !== 0) {\n      throw new Error(`npm install failed with code ${result.status}. See ${logPath}`);\n    }\n    NODE_INSTALL_DIR = installDir;\n    // Add to NODE_PATH and re-init module paths\n    process.env.NODE_PATH = path.join(installDir, 'node_modules');\n    const Module = require('module');\n    Module._initPaths();\n    console.log('Dependencies installed and module paths updated.');\n  }\n}","new_string":"// Ensure dependencies\nfunction ensureDependencies() {\n  console.log('Checking dependencies...');\n  try {\n    require('canvas');\n    console.log('canvas already available.');\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log('canvas not found. Installing dependencies to temp dir...');\n    const installDir = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'openclaw_node_modules');\n    if (!fs.existsSync(installDir)) fs.mkdirSync(installDir, { recursive: true });\n\n    // Use npm with shell option to handle .cmd on Windows\n    const args = ['install', '--prefix', installDir, 'pdfjs-dist', 'canvas'];\n    const result = spawnSync('npm', args, { cwd: installDir, stdio: 'pipe', encoding: 'utf-8', shell: true });\n    const logPath = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'npm-install.log');\n    if (result.stdout) fs.writeFileSync(logPath, result.stdout);\n    if (result.stderr) fs.appendFileSync(logPath, result.stderr);\n    if (result.status !== 0) {\n      throw new Error(`npm install failed with code ${result.status}. See ${logPath}`);\n    }\n    NODE_INSTALL_DIR = installDir;\n    // Add to NODE_PATH and re-init module paths\n    process.env.NODE_PATH = path.join(installDir, 'node_modules');\n    const Module = require('module');\n    Module._initPaths();\n    console.log('Dependencies installed and module paths updated.');\n  }\n}"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":87916,"output":3320,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":91236,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419439509}}
