erences, causing JSON.stringify to fail? No.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the script ran out of memory or something causing a non-graceful exit? exit code 1 could be from uncaught exception.\n\nLet's add more specific error handling around the render step and also ensure we log everything before exiting. We already have.\n\nPerhaps the script is crashing before it reaches the `await renderFirstPage()`? Wait, after loading PDF, we have:\n\n```javascript\nconst imageData = await renderFirstPage();\n```\n\nrenderFirstPage is defined earlier. Inside it, we have:\n\nawait page.render(...).promise;\n\nIf that throws, the await will throw, and the exception propagates to the try block, caught, and we log error. So we should see error.\n\nBut we see no error. Could it be that the script crashed before reaching the catch due to an unhandled rejection from something else? Let's examine the entire code flow: main is async. We call main() and don't handle its promise rejection at top-level. However, inside main we have a try/catch that wraps all the code. So any exception in the async function should be caught. That includes awaited calls.\n\nUnless something throws outside the try, like a module load error after loadExternalModules? But we already loaded modules.\n\nMaybe the error occurs after the script finishes but before we capture the log? No.\n\nGiven the difficulty, I'll try to run the script without pty but capture output via redirecting to a file, and then read the file. Since we suspect pty might be mangling output. But earlier non-pty gave no output at all. Maybe we need to not use background, just exec and wait for completion, and the exec tool returns output in its response? The exec tool's docs: \"Execute shell commands with background continuation.\" Without background, it likely runs synchronously and returns output. However earlier we tried exec without background and got no output. But maybe we didn't set `pty=true`. Without pty, output might not be captured. With pty we get output but mangled.\n\nLet's try exec without background but with pty? Maybe then we get output in the response. But we need non-blocking? Actually, exec without background should block until completion and return output. However, the tool signature doesn't have a \"blocking\" parameter; by default it's not background? The background param defaults to false. If we don't set background, it should execute and wait, then return output. But earlier we did `exec(command=\"echo test\")` and got no output. That suggests maybe the exec tool's response does not include stdout; it only returns when backgrounded? Hmm.\n\nLet's read the tool description more: \"Execute shell commands with background continuation. Use yieldMs/background to continue later via process tool.\" This suggests that if you set background=true, it runs in background and you later poll. If you don't set background, it might run synchronously and return output? But the examples in docs? Not sure.\n\nMaybe the exec tool always returns immediately with a session ID, and you must use process to get output. That's what we've been doing.\n\nGiven that, we need to parse the raw PTY output to see the error. But it's messy. Instead, we could have the script write errors to a separate file that we can read regardless of output capture. In the catch block, we can write the error to a file in TEMP_DIR. That way we can read it.\n\nI'll modify the catch to write error details to a file.\n\nSomething like:\n\n```javascript\n} catch (err) {\n  const errorPath = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'analysis-error.txt');\n  fs.writeFileSync(errorPath, `${err.message}\\n${err.stack}\\n`);\n  console.error('\\n===STATUS===ERROR');\n  console.error(err.message);\n  console.error(err.stack);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n```\n\nThen we can read that file.\n\nAlso, we could write a debug file after each major step.\n\nI'll update the script accordingly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll enhance error logging to a file to see what went wrong:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_413764092067458cae03fed8","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social\\analyze-and-generate.js","old_string":"// Main\nasync function main() {\n  console.log('=== Starting PDF analysis and slide generation ===');\n  let themeCssContent = null;\n  let pdfContent = null;\n\n  try {\n    ensureDependencies();\n    loadExternalModules();\n    checkPdfExists();\n\n    const imageData = await renderFirstPage();\n    const dominantColors = analyzeColors(imageData);\n    console.log('Dominant colors:', dominantColors.map(c => `rgb(${c.r},${c.g},${c.b})`).join(', '));\n\n    const layoutInfo = await analyzeLayout();\n    console.log('Layout info:', JSON.stringify(layoutInfo, null, 2));\n\n    const css = generateTheme(dominantColors, layoutInfo);\n    themeCssContent = css;\n\n    const { generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath } = locateResources();\n    runSlideGenerator(generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath, CONFIG.themeCssPath, CONFIG.outputPdfPath);\n\n    if (!fs.existsSync(CONFIG.outputPdfPath)) {\n      throw new Error('Slide generator did not produce output PDF');\n    }\n    pdfContent = fs.readFileSync(CONFIG.outputPdfPath);\n    console.log('PDF generated, size:', pdfContent.length, 'bytes');\n\n    // Output base64 for agent capture\n    console.log('\\n===THEME_CSS_BASE64===');\n    console.log(Buffer.from(themeCssContent).toString('base64'));\n    console.log('\\n===PDF_BASE64===');\n    console.log(pdfContent.toString('base64'));\n    console.log('\\n===STATUS===SUCCESS');\n    console.log('Completed successfully.');\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error('\\n===STATUS===ERROR');\n    console.error(err.message);\n    console.error(err.stack);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n\nmain();","new_string":"// Main\nasync function main() {\n  console.log('=== Starting PDF analysis and slide generation ===');\n  let themeCssContent = null;\n  let pdfContent = null;\n\n  try {\n    ensureDependencies();\n    loadExternalModules();\n    checkPdfExists();\n\n    const imageData = await renderFirstPage();\n    const dominantColors = analyzeColors(imageData);\n    console.log('Dominant colors:', dominantColors.map(c => `rgb(${c.r},${c.g},${c.b})`).join(', '));\n\n    const layoutInfo = await analyzeLayout();\n    console.log('Layout info:', JSON.stringify(layoutInfo, null, 2));\n\n    const css = generateTheme(dominantColors, layoutInfo);\n    themeCssContent = css;\n\n    const { generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath } = locateResources();\n    runSlideGenerator(generatorPath, exampleSlidesPath, CONFIG.themeCssPath, CONFIG.outputPdfPath);\n\n    if (!fs.existsSync(CONFIG.outputPdfPath)) {\n      throw new Error('Slide generator did not produce output PDF');\n    }\n    pdfContent = fs.readFileSync(CONFIG.outputPdfPath);\n    console.log('PDF generated, size:', pdfContent.length, 'bytes');\n\n    // Output base64 for agent capture\n    console.log('\\n===THEME_CSS_BASE64===');\n    console.log(Buffer.from(themeCssContent).toString('base64'));\n    console.log('\\n===PDF_BASE64===');\n    console.log(pdfContent.toString('base64'));\n    console.log('\\n===STATUS===SUCCESS');\n    console.log('Completed successfully.');\n  } catch (err) {\n    // Write error details to a file for debugging\n    const errorPath = path.join(TEMP_DIR, 'analysis-error.txt');\n    try {\n      fs.writeFileSync(errorPath, `Error: ${err.message}\\nStack: ${err.stack}\\n`);\n    } catch (e) {}\n    console.error('\\n===STATUS===ERROR');\n    console.error(err.message);\n    console.error(err.stack);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n\nmain();"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":109347,"output":7474,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":116821,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419688471}}
