{"type":"message","id":"1d6611f9","parentId":"7e9ccc9b","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:03:52.429Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Canvas test passed. So canvas works. The crash occurs after \"PDF loaded: 12 pages.\" That is after `await loadingTask.promise` and before any further log. The next operation is `const page = await pdf.getPage(1);`. That is inside renderFirstPage after we call it. The canvas test is before calling renderFirstPage. So the crash likely happens in `await renderFirstPage()`.\n\nSpecifically, inside renderFirstPage, the first line after entering is `const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument(CONFIG.pdfPath);` That returns immediately. Then we do `const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;`. Wait, we already did that in main? Actually, we already loaded the PDF in main? No, we did not. In main we called `checkPdfExists()` but not loading. The loading happens in renderFirstPage. But the log \"PDF loaded: 12 pages.\" is inside renderFirstPage after `await loadingTask.promise`. So that line logged from renderFirstPage, not from main. That means renderFirstPage executed up to that point. After that, the next line is `const page = await pdf.getPage(1);`. That is where the error likely occurs. So `pdf.getPage(1)` might be throwing.\n\nMaybe the page number is invalid? But PDF has 12 pages, page 1 should exist. Could be that the pdf object is not fully ready? But getDocument().promise resolves when PDF is loaded, and then you can call getPage.\n\nMaybe the error is that the page's viewport is huge and creating canvas fails? But that's after getPage.\n\nSo we need to catch errors in renderFirstPage specifically. We have a try/catch in main that should catch any error from renderFirstPage. But we aren't seeing it. Possibly because renderFirstPage throws an error that is not caught by our try/catch because it's thrown after an await that is not inside the try? But it is inside the try.\n\nLet's re-check the main: try { ... const imageData = await renderFirstPage(); ... } catch (err) { ... }. That should catch any error from renderFirstPage.\n\nSo if getPage throws, it should be caught and logged. But we see no error log. That suggests that maybe the error occurs after the catch block? No.\n\nMaybe the error is thrown not as an exception but as a process exit due to something like an unhandled 'error' event on some stream? For example, the canvas creation might emit an error event and then crash? But createCanvas succeeded in test.\n\nMaybe the page.render call is not reached because getPage threw. But still caught.\n\nGiven we see \"PDF loaded: 12 pages.\" and then immediately process exit with code 1, perhaps the process called `process.exit(1)` somewhere else, maybe inside pdfjs-dist on error? pdfjs-dist might call process.exit if something fatal? Unlikely.\n\nMaybe there is an unhandled rejection in the `page.render` promise that occurs after we've already left the function? But we haven't called it yet.\n\nLet's add more logging inside renderFirstPage to pinpoint exactly where it fails. We'll modify renderFirstPage to log before and after each step.\n\nI'll rewrite renderFirstPage with try/catch inside and rethrow.\n\nBut first, maybe the issue is that after we did `await loadingTask.promise` (first await in renderFirstPage), we are no longer in the main's try? Actually we are, because the function is called from main.\n\nI'll add a try/catch in renderFirstPage that logs and rethrows.\n\nLet's modify:\n\n```javascript\nasync function renderFirstPage() {\n  console.log('renderFirstPage: start');\n  try {\n    console.log('Loading PDF...');\n    const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument(CONFIG.pdfPath);\n    console.log('Got loading task');\n    const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\n    console.log(`PDF loaded: ${pdf.numPages} pages.`);\n    console.log('Getting page 1...');\n    const page = await pdf.getPage(1);\n    console.log('Got page 1');\n    const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1.0 });\n    console.log('Got viewport', viewport.width, viewport.height);\n    const canvas = createCanvas(viewport.width, viewport.height);\n    console.log('Created canvas');\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n    console.log('Got context');\n    await page.render({ canvasContext: ctx, viewport }).promise;\n    console.log('Render complete.');\n    const imageData = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n    console.log('Got image data');\n    return { data: imageData.data, width: canvas.width, height: canvas.height };\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.error('renderFirstPage error:', e);\n    throw e;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis will give detailed logs.\n\nLet's update.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll add detailed logging to renderFirstPage to pinpoint the failure:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_16e2851e940c4a69a1467781","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-social\\analyze-and-generate.js","old_string":"// Render first page\nasync function renderFirstPage() {\n  console.log('Loading PDF...');\n  const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument(CONFIG.pdfPath);\n  const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\n  console.log(`PDF loaded: ${pdf.numPages} pages.`);\n  const page = await pdf.getPage(1);\n  const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1.0 });\n  const canvas = createCanvas(viewport.width, viewport.height);\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n  await page.render({ canvasContext: ctx, viewport }).promise;\n  console.log('First page rendered to canvas.');\n  const imageData = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  return { data: imageData.data, width: canvas.width, height: canvas.height };\n}","new_string":"// Render first page\nasync function renderFirstPage() {\n  console.log('renderFirstPage: start');\n  try {\n    console.log('Loading PDF...');\n    const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument(CONFIG.pdfPath);\n    console.log('Got loading task');\n    const pdf = await loadingTask.promise;\n    console.log(`PDF loaded: ${pdf.numPages} pages.`);\n    console.log('Getting page 1...');\n    const page = await pdf.getPage(1);\n    console.log('Got page 1');\n    const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1.0 });\n    console.log('Got viewport', viewport.width, viewport.height);\n    const canvas = createCanvas(viewport.width, viewport.height);\n    console.log('Created canvas');\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n    console.log('Got context');\n    await page.render({ canvasContext: ctx, viewport }).promise;\n    console.log('Render complete.');\n    const imageData = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n    console.log('Got image data');\n    return { data: imageData.data, width: canvas.width, height: canvas.height };\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.error('renderFirstPage error:', e);\n    throw e;\n  }\n}"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":119011,"output":2758,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":121769,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771419816389}}
